    {
      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "To determine the number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy, we need to consider all combinations of entrees, drinks, and desserts. Let's break it down step by step:\n\n1. **Identify the options for each category:**\n   - Entrees: Pizza, Chicken Teriyaki, Corn Dog, Fish and Chips\n   - Drinks: Lemonade, Root Beer\n   - Desserts: Frozen Yogurt, Chocolate Chip Cookie\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of combinations:**\n   - For each entree, Crystal can choose any of the 4 entrees.\n   - For each drink, she can choose any of the 2 drinks.\n   - For each dessert, she can choose any of the 2 desserts.\n\n   Therefore, the total number of distinct possible meals is the product of the number of choices for each category:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total combinations} = (\\text{Number of entrees}) \\times (\\text{Number of drinks}) \\times (\\text{Number of desserts})\n   \\]\n\n   Substituting the values we have:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total combinations} = 4 \\times 2 \\times 2\n   \\]\n\n3. **Perform the multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   4 \\times 2 = 8\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   8 \\times 2 = 16\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{16}\n\\]",
