      "text": "To determine the number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy, we need to calculate the total number of combinations of entrees, drinks, and desserts she can choose from. \n\n1. **Entrees:** There are 4 entrees available (Pizza, Chicken Teriyaki, Corn Dog, and Fish and Chips). \n\n2. **Drinks:** There are 2 drink options (Lemonade and Root Beer).\n\n3. **Desserts:** There are 2 dessert options (Frozen Yogurt and Chocolate Chip Cookie).\n\nTo find the total number of distinct possible meals, we multiply the number of choices for each category:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total meals} = (\\text{Number of entrees}) \\times (\\text{Number of drinks}) \\times (\\text{Number of desserts})\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total meals} = 4 \\times 2 \\times 2\n\\]\n\nNow, calculate the product:\n\n\\[\n4 \\times 2 = 8\n\\]\n\\[\n8 \\times 2 = 16\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{16}\n\\]",
